{
  "id": 504134899,
  "iid": 25698,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "hosts: Add base personal hosts file to name resolution load order",
  "description": "Previously, hosts files were loaded in this order:\n1. Global hosts file (e.g. `C:\\Program Files\\Wireshark\\hosts`)\n2. Profile hosts file (e.g. `%APPDATA%\\Wireshark\\profiles\\<name>\\hosts`)\n\nThis change adds a third hosts file location, making the new load order:\n1. Global hosts file (e.g. `C:\\Program Files\\Wireshark\\hosts`)\n2. Base personal hosts file (e.g. `%APPDATA%\\Wireshark\\hosts`)\n3. Profile hosts file (e.g. `%APPDATA%\\Wireshark\\profiles\\<name>\\hosts`)\n\nSince the last file loaded wins on conflicting entries, this gives a\nthree-tier precedence: enterprise/global > user-wide personal (this change) > per-profile.\n\nMany users do not have write access to system directories like\n`Program Files`, leaving the profile hosts file as their only option.\nThis forces them to duplicate entries across every profile. The new base\npersonal hosts file provides a single place to maintain user-wide name\nresolution overrides that apply across all profiles, while still allowing\nindividual profiles to override them.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes",
  "state": "merged",
